# Cognos adapter (consume, do not invent)

How-to + owner catalogue: `_____________KDB3API/contracts/cognosHostService.md` **§0**. Catalogue of who stamps which facet: **§7**. Design origin (outside this root): `ADAPTER_ONTWERP_2026-08-20.md`.

Three folders named “cognos” are not one layer. Do not merge them.

| Layer | Folder | May call | Must not |
|---|---|---|---|
| Inner ring | `core/cognosAPI/` | `__getDashboardAPI()` | feature flow, state |
| Ring 1 | `core/services/cognosHost/` | `_KDB.cognosAPI.*` | `__getDashboardAPI()` |
| Chrome | `core/cognosHost/` | selectors / chrome checks | SDK / facets |
| Feature, writeback `get/` `set/` `effects/`, other services | owner module | stamped `_KDB.runtime.<owner>.*Facet` via `effects/read*Facet.js` | `_KDB.cognosAPI`, `__getDashboardAPI()`, deep `_KDB.services.cognosHost` lookup |

```js
// orchestrator (once)
_KDB.runtime.widgetVis.dataQueryFacet = _KDB.services.cognosHost.dataQuery;

// effect — read the stamp, not the service
var facet = (_KDB.runtime.widgetVis || {}).dataQueryFacet;
facet.peekQueryRows(/* ids/DTOs */); // Outcome, never a host Promise/handle
```

Exceptions (do not copy): PDF `captureTabPage.js` → `resolveCaptureRoot`; `KDB.js` namespace mount/unmount; dienststelle’s **one** named filters choke in §7.

Do **not** add a facet or facet op without PO + contract + a live `KDB3/js/**` caller (D4). Stale feature-contract sentences that still say “call `_KDB.cognosAPI`” lose to this rule and to §0. `runtime.<owner>.adapters` is not the Cognos facet path.
